WEBVTT

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.440
Oh, come on! You're hanging on him again?

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.480
<i>Just punch already!</i>

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.580
We didn't pay to see two men dancing cheek-to-cheek!

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:28.520
Hit him!

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.530
Give us a better fight than that!

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.030
<i>Rush him! Do it! Do it!</i>

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.780
Yeah! Kick his ass six ways to Sunday!

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.870
This ain't kickboxing, you idiot!

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:39.740
Yeah, that's it! Hit him! Hit him!

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:41.660
Way to go, Hurricane! Don't let up now!

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:42.410
Rush him!

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.250
Now! Aim for the body! The body!

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:47.410
Keep your eyes peeled, c'mon!

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.460
Yeah! Body! The Body!

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.380
Go! Hit his body!

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:54.300
Get him!

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.720
You're not actually taking this seriously, are you, moron?

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:03.680
Sorry, Joe was just spurring me on.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:06.680
Come on, stop clinching! Hit him!

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:07.520
Punch him!

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:08.390
Fight!

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:11.150
Go! Use your legs!

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.400
Hurricane! Fight! Fight!

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.690
Hey, Yabuki! What do you think you're doing?

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.320
We can't have our star show himself in front of the audience yet!

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.710
Fine, fine.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:25.920
Just stop pushing!

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.210
Sure is hard being the star, huh?

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.180
What the hell are you doing, idiot? This ain't wrestling!

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.770
<i>No, no, that's no good!</i>

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.470
Come on! Start using uppercuts!

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.470
Uppercuts! You hear me?

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:49.520
Cut that out, idiot!

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.980
Since when did you join the audience?

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:52.940
Listen up, folks!

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.240
I've got good news! Though we didn't exactly sell out,

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.200
a whole lot of spectators still showed up.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:03.870
If this keeps up, you all may get your long-awaited bonus when they hold their festival.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:08.710
A bonus? That's not that big a deal...

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.710
especially when it's only five yen!

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.050
Don't be ridiculous!

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.220
If we don't draw an audience, you can forget about bonuses!

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.340
Hell, you'll be out in the cold!

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:25.810
Now, give us a good match and entertain the crowd, got it?

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:26.310
Okay.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.270
What the hell are you doing?

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:32.980
Go! Go! Attack!

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.740
Shut the hell up! You sound like a kid!

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:36.610
Pull yourself together, new guy!

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:40.110
You talking to me?

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.610
You see any other new guys around here?

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.700
Is there a rule that says I can't watch the matches?

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:54.500
It's not like you getting excited will do anything for the guys in the ring.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.210
So just keep it down.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:57.880
What?

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:03.600
It's just that we touring types have our own way of doing things.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.890
Show us what you got!

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:07.100
Here!

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.310
Looks like it's gonna rain.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.150
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.240
Take too long and I'll kill you!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:18.360
It's cold.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.320
Hey. It's started to rain.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.570
Take the fall already.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:26.070
Don't you think it's too obvious if I fall over, just like that?

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.580
Don't worry. This grass-lot league ain't even approved by the commissioner.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.410
You got a point.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.630
Way to go, Señor! You got him!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.130
Way to go!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.850
<i>Stop!</i>

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.140
Take that!

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.840
What the hell?

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.900
Yeah! You did it! Way to go, Hurricane!

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:59.320
What the hell are you wasting time for?

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.280
You've raised his hand, now get on with it!

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.280
<i>Get out of the ring!</i>

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.830
Bring out Joe the Killer, the guy that beat Rikiishi to death!

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:08.280
Do it now, before the rain gets worse!

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.580
Get out of here now, or I'll beat you to death!

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:16.080
Okay, Yabuki-kun. The audience is here only for you.

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:20.340
Just get into the ring, dish out some killer punches, and take out your opponent.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.550
That'll satisfy the audience.

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:24.680
Go give us a good show now.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.760
That was what I was planning on doing all along.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.600
Let's not forget the rain.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:35.900
Finish it off quickly, for both of our sakes.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:39.860
I was just thinking the same thing.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.990
But I don't think it'll be that easy.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:43.730
All depends on my opponent.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:49.450
Don't you worry. I've given your opponent his instructions.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.120
Instructions?

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:59.580
Hey. Somebody bring me my gloves.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.590
You mean I have to fight him?

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:09.390
You're gonna exchange blows until the last fifteen seconds of the first round.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:12.300
The referee will give you a signal when there's fifteen seconds left.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:20.310
Then you'll let loose the terrifying Cross Counter that drove the whole country wild.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.780
And Inaba-kun will go down.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.320
He won't even move a muscle.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.420
So, this is a fixed match?

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.800
Then I refuse.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.050
Wh-Where do you get the nerve!

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:49.800
Are you defying your promoter?

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.970
Are you suggesting that I fight a fixed match?

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:56.770
H-Hey, I can't...

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:57.940
Hey. Don't.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:06:59.150
But Inaba-san...

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.080
Get on with it!

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.860
Get out here, Joe!

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:07.570
Come on, Killer!

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.450
How long do we have to wait in the rain?

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.070
Start the goddamn match!

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:14.580
Bring out Joe the Killer!

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:17.080
Get on with it!

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.840
H-Hold on a second!

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:30.340
We'll start the match as soon as both fighters are ready, so just wait a little bit longer.

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:34.220
It's not like they're putting on a damn wedding dress!

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.310
How long does it take to put on a pair of trunks?

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:40.100
I don't care if he's naked! Just get him out here!

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:44.190
Look at him!

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.710
Looking good, boss!

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.360
Bring him out already!

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:51.330
Inaba-san...

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:53.700
I want to trust you.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.500
You used to be a pretty competent boxer, didn't you?

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.750
Even though you've degraded yourself into a touring boxer,

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:03.590
you wouldn't taint boxing itself by fighting a fixed match.

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:05.460
Would you?

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:21.430
You better stay in line, Yabuki.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.650
This ain't no kids' fight.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.210
<i>We apologize for the delay!</i>

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:47.210
<i>We will now begin our main event...</i>

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:51.800
Who gives a crap? Start the fight already!

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.470
Okay then...

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.350
Inaba-san...

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.690
I don't care what script they gave you to follow.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:08.030
Come on! Get moving!

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.280
Yeah! Go get him!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:58.570
Looks like you've avoided fighting a fixed match.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.910
And that's a <i>Pon</i>!

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.620
Here!

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.370
Are you sure? That's a <i>Dora</i>, you know.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:47.910
Oh, a <i>Dora</i>?

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:51.250
I'd really like to play this, but how?

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.140
Whatever, just make your move!

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:04.970
I did it! That's an <i>Oyaman</i>!

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:05.850
Thank you!

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:16.270
I'm out of luck today. First I lose money at cards, now Mahjong's a no-go.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.530
Looks like the Bear turns into a sitting duck whenever it rains.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:24.870
Yeah, I hate this weather. It's like we're back to square one.{meaning? tlc}

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.790
Hey, old man! You think we're still on for our match tomorrow?

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.130
We're gonna run dry if the weather doesn't clear up.

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:35.090
You don't need a sword to kill us. Just three rainy days is enough.

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:38.840
Okay, you drew it! Now play your tile already!

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:45.970
Yeah, new guy? You want something?

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:50.270
You've been staring at me this whole time! It's creeping me out!

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:52.940
Why don't you tell me if you want something?

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.270
All right, jerkoff?{"faggot" from TL - tlc needed}

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:58.320
I wasn't looking at you, you know.

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:02.320
Then why were you looking my way with that condescending look?

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:05.780
I was just watching the guy behind you.

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.870
You got a problem with that?

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:22.220
Why the hell does the former second-ranked featherweight

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:25.930
have to fight these fixed matches?

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.390
He's not like any of these chumps.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:32.980
Wh-What the hell? Are you calling us chumps?

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.780
I let you talk, and you start mouthing off, huh, brat?

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:38.190
You're nothing more than a greenhorn to us!

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:43.280
This is Shark Suzuki, Raiden Tamegoro, and me, Bear Minezaki, the Middleweight Trio!

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:44.650
Who the hell do you take us for?

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.700
That wasn't what I meant.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.250
I don't care that this is a touring grass-lot league.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.380
I'm saying that anyone who'd fight a fixed match

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:54.660
has no right to wear gloves!

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:55.840
Now you've said it, brat!

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:56.460
Punk!

00:12:57.340 --> 00:12:58.920
H-hold on a second there!

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.090
Do you have any idea what you're saying?

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:02.050
Let's say someone got injured!

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.010
We'd be right out of business!

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.970
You keep talking about fixed matches,

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.600
but we think of it as a kind of show.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:13.150
And shows have to be entertaining.

00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:15.820
You really gotta get that!

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:16.520
I don't get it.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:17.520
I don't fucking get it!

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:25.830
You don't need to tell me to put on a scripted show for the hicks. All of my matches...

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:28.530
will end in a KO in the first round.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:29.790
Son of a-

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:30.790
We'll kill you!

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:33.670
Cut it out! No point in fighting now!

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:35.620
Save the fighting for the ring!

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:36.250
Shaddap!

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:40.750
Hold it!

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:47.140
You guys making a ruckus in here will spoil my sake.{no need for italics i think}

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:48.930
If you're gonna fight, do it outside.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:51.680
But it's raining out there!

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:56.060
If you can't fight in the rain, then don't fight at all.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.780
Did you hear what I just said!?

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:15.750
Then sit back down and play your game.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.910
And Joe, you try to be quiet when it's raining.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:22.170
You're not a kid anymore.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:05.880
Azuki beans!

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:51.970
Well? You wanna take a bit of a walk?

00:15:52.350 --> 00:15:53.100
Sure.

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:10.900
Don't you love summer festivals?

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:12.900
Yeah.

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:17.620
Don't be so quick to judge.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.870
They're still a good bunch, you know.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:23.000
Yeah.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:34.760
Come one, come all!

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.010
It's almost time to start!

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:38.930
Come see the raw thrills you can't get from the TV!

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:41.310
How many people can Joe the Killer kill today?

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:43.480
Come one, come all!

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:55.990
Today's draw is how many consecutive KOs Joe can get.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:59.530
You and you, get knocked out in the first round. Got it?

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.420
You guys stick to the plan.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:06.790
You'll get compensated if you get roughed up a little.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:07.550
Right.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.720
I'll be counting on you, Inaba-kun.

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:14.260
Now, remember, Joe, they're all our precious performers.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.430
Don't hurt them too much.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:17.180
Yeah.

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:22.190
You won't knock me out that easily!

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:22.810
Damn right!

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.110
I'll take him out with my own power!

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:26.560
And if you can't, I will.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:27.860
And if I can't...

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:28.820
Moron!

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:31.150
I can do it all myself.

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:34.200
I'm not gonna lose to that punk. Just watch me.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:39.070
Yeah! This time, we're turning down the fixed match!

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:49.040
Come on, come on! What's the matter?

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.670
Is that all you got? This is hardly even a show!

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:00.180
Yeah, Joe! That's the way!

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:01.890
That idiot punched him for real!

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:02.680
Okay, next!

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.820
Yeah! Go get 'em, Joe!

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:25.330
Dear God...

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:26.830
That bastard's getting full of himself!

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:27.840
Hold on a second, Joe!

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:28.880
Wh-What do you want?

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.050
Get out of the ring!

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:30.840
B-But...

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:33.590
Come on, I'm hardly breaking a sweat!

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:36.390
That's not it! We have a problem! A big problem!

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:37.850
Just look over here...

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:45.600
They're all gonna be out of commission for a while!

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:49.020
I just gave them a love tap, that's all.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:51.600
I guess this is what happens when you fight fixed matches instead of practicing.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:53.610
Damn...

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:54.780
I'm begging you here!

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:57.490
We'll have to fire the fighters you knocked out,

00:18:57.490 --> 00:19:01.410
but damage any more of them, and we can't replace them!

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:02.620
Please, Joe...

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:07.290
S-Sir, don't do something so cruel as to leave me behind...

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:09.330
I've got to send money back to my mother...

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:11.710
This pain is nothing to me!

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:13.010
I'll be better soon!

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:15.760
Please, don't fire us!

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:18.430
I-I can be back on my feet by tomorrow!

00:19:18.430 --> 00:19:20.180
Come on, please!

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:22.930
What are you talking about?

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:24.680
I'm not paying anyone who can't fight!

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:27.100
Come on, get on with it! It's getting late!

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:28.600
Okay, Shark, you're up next.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:30.600
Y-Yes, sir...

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.980
Go on, Joe. Do it like I said.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:39.570
Hold it, Shark.

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.580
I'll go in the ring next.

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:48.330
B-But Inaba-san, you're supposed to be last!

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:52.170
Come on, old man. Don't be so stiff!

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:53.830
Either way, I'm up next.

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:01.760
All we have to do is give the audience an entertaining match, right?

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:02.840
Well? What do you say?

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:04.850
Y-Yeah, you've got a point...

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:08.350
Then I'll go up next.

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:31.080
No need to hold back, Yabuki.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:33.960
Okay then, here I come!

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.350
This is real damn intense!

00:20:51.690 --> 00:20:54.360
It's worth every penny!

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:24.140
Yeah, that's the way! Get him! Get him!

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:43.030
B-Been a while since I've felt a punch in my bones like this.

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:24.610
You okay, Inaba-san?

00:22:26.410 --> 00:22:27.990
I'll live.

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:32.160
That pain brought back memories for me.

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:36.000
Next time we fight, let's do it like that.

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:42.260
But pull your punches a bit when you fight the others.

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:45.510
Sure.

00:22:49.510 --> 00:22:53.560
Either way, I can tell you won't be touring much longer.

00:22:57.730 --> 00:22:59.560
One more thing, Joe.

00:22:59.560 --> 00:23:03.610
Isn't someone waiting for you to come home?

00:24:39.120 --> 00:24:43.120
Joe gets a day off from touring, and climbs a mountain deep in the countryside.

00:24:43.590 --> 00:24:48.340
When Joe gets lost in the mist, he is helped by a ranch girl named Yuri.

00:24:48.340 --> 00:24:55.130
Yuri lives with her kind mother on this lush, green ranch where cows and horses roam free.

00:24:55.160 --> 00:25:00.940
Joe feels the gentle gaze, smile, and love of a mother for the first time.

00:25:00.940 --> 00:25:04.900
Now, as Joe chases after the distant face of his mother,

00:25:04.900 --> 00:25:06.530
which way is tomorrow!?
